    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.10.266": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, English (Pre-19th Century Literature)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, English (Pre-19th Century Literature) - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Assistant Professor, English (Pre-19th Century Literature) Department of English, Faculty of Arts and Science Competition No. 26.10.266 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Tenure-Track Commensurate with qualifications and experience. New hires will normally be placed within the first 8 steps of the Assistant Professor salary table. A review of applications will begin November 15, 2026 and continue until a suitable candidate is found. Category Full-Time Tenure-Track Salary Commensurate with qualifications and experience. New hires will normally be placed within the first 8 steps of the Assistant Professor salary table. Closing Date A review of applications will begin November 15, 2026 and continue until a suitable candidate is found. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity The Department of English in the Faculty of Arts and Science invites applications for an entry-level, full-time, tenure-track appointment in pre-19th Century Literature at the rank of Assistant Professor, commencing July 1, 2027, subject to final budgetary approval. The Department of English is seeking an outstanding teacher with a scholarly research background in pre-19th century literature. While we are open to all pre-19th century periods, our preference is for either Medieval literature or 18th-century literature. The successful candidate should present an ongoing research plan, demonstrate a commitment to undergraduate education, and provide evidence of teaching excellence at the post-secondary level. For details about our department and the areas of expertise of our faculty members, see https://www.macewan.ca/academics/academic-departments/english/ . You will teach senior-level courses in your period of expertise and introductory literature and/or writing courses, as well as develop special topics courses and seminars in pre-19th century literature. You will also engage in scholarship as appropriate to your disciplinary background and in academic service to your department or faculty. You must have, or be close to completion of, a terminal degree (Ph.D.) in English (or in a relevant area of expertise) and will demonstrate a primary commitment to undergraduate teaching and an ongoing research program. You will submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching dossier (including recent teaching evaluations), statement of research interests, and sample of scholarly work. Only shortlisted candidates will be contacted by the Department Chair to provide three (3) letters of reference sent directly from referees. Only selected candidates will be required to submit official transcripts sent directly from the institutions where you completed your degrees. Questions about this opportunity may be addressed to Dr. Lana Krys, Department Chair, at kryss@macewan.ca. How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the Faculty Association collective agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.10.259": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Indigegogy",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Indigegogy - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Assistant Professor, Indigegogy Faculty of Arts and Science Competition No. 26.10.259 Posting Date October 20, 2026 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Tenure-Track Commensurate with qualifications and experience.\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNew hires will normally be placed within the first 8 steps of the Assistant Professor salary table. A review of applications will begin November 15, 2026 and continue until a suitable candidate is found. Category Full-Time Tenure-Track Salary Commensurate with qualifications and experience.\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNew hires will normally be placed within the first 8 steps of the Assistant Professor salary table. Closing Date A review of applications will begin November 15, 2026 and continue until a suitable candidate is found. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity The Faculty of Arts and Science invites applications for an entry-level, full-time, tenure-track appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor, commencing July 1, 2027, subject to final budgetary approval. The Faculty is seeking a faculty member with Indigenous lived experience who is grounded in Indigenous ways of knowing, being, and doing, and who can contribute to the teaching and scholarly mission of one or more departments, depending on the disciplinary expertise of the candidate. You will teach courses in your area of expertise, as well as contribute to course offerings in our Indigegogy minor. Built through consultation with Indigenous scholars and Knowledge Keepers, the Indigegogy minor offers a unique, multi-disciplinary program that puts Indigenous knowledge, experience and cultural perspectives at the heart of the program. The Faculty is committed to expanding our curriculum to incorporate Indigenous perspectives and ways of knowing, and as such will consider applicants from the full range of disciplines represented in the BA and BSc. For details about our disciplines, see Programs - MacEwan University . You will teach six courses per year in our BA and/or BSc programs, as well as engage in scholarship or creative activity as appropriate to your disciplinary background. You will also engage in academic service to your department or Faculty. You will demonstrate a primary commitment to undergraduate teaching and an ongoing research program. Having, or being close to completion of, a terminal degree in your area of expertise is preferred. You will submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching dossier (including recent teaching evaluations or other proof of effective teaching), statement of research interests, and sample of scholarly work. Only shortlisted candidates will be contacted by the Department Chair to provide three (3) letters of reference sent directly from referees. Only selected candidates will be required to submit official transcripts sent directly from the institutions where you completed your degrees. Shortlisted candidates may also be asked to provide evidence of their ability to collaborate with Indigenous communities through examples of previous collaboration, or a letter of support from an Indigenous community. Questions about this opportunity may be addressed to Kevin Friesen, Associate Dean, Operations, at FriesenK8@macewan.ca . How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the Faculty Association collective agreement All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.10.258": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Political Science",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Political Science - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Assistant Professor, Political Science Department of Anthropology, Economics, and Political Science, Faculty of Arts and Science Competition No. 26.10.258 Posting Date October 20, 2026 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Tenure-Track Commensurate with qualifications and experience. New hires will normally be placed within the first 8 steps of the Assistant Professor salary table. A review of applications will begin November 15, 2026 and continue until a suitable candidate is found. Category Full-Time Tenure-Track Salary Commensurate with qualifications and experience. New hires will normally be placed within the first 8 steps of the Assistant Professor salary table. Closing Date A review of applications will begin November 15, 2026 and continue until a suitable candidate is found. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity The Department of Anthropology, Economics, and Political Science in the Faculty of Arts and Science invites applications for an entry-level, full-time, tenure-track appointment in Political Science, in the field of Canadian Politics at the rank of Assistant Professor, commencing July 1, 2027, subject to final budgetary approval. This is a teaching, research, and service position, with a normal teaching load of six courses per year at all levels of the curriculum. Preferred candidates will have post-secondary teaching experience that provides evidence of excellence or promise of excellence in teaching. The ability to teach in more than one sub-field, supported by an ongoing research program, is an asset. You will teach six courses per year, carry out an ongoing research program, and provide service to the University. You must have, or be close to completion of, a terminal degree in Political Science, and an ongoing research program relevant to the teaching of Canadian Politics. You will submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching dossier (including recent teaching evaluations), statement of research interests, and sample of scholarly work. Only shortlisted candidates will be contacted by the Department Chair to provide three (3) letters of reference sent directly from referees. Only selected candidates will be required to submit official transcripts sent directly from the institutions where you completed your degrees. Questions about this opportunity may be addressed to Gaelan Murphy, Department Chair, at murphyc23@macewan.ca . How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the Faculty Association collective agreement All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.10.264": {
      "title": "Lab Supervisor, Biological Sciences",
      "description": "Lab Supervisor, Biological Sciences - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Lab Supervisor, Biological Sciences Department of Biological Sciences,  Faculty of Arts and Science Competition No. 26.10.264 Posting Date October 22, 2026 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Tenure-Track Commensurate with qualifications and experience.  New hires will normally be placed within the first 5 steps of the Lab Supervisors salary table. A review of applications will begin November 15, 2026 and continue until a suitable candidate is found. Category Full-Time Tenure-Track Salary Commensurate with qualifications and experience.  New hires will normally be placed within the first 5 steps of the Lab Supervisors salary table. Closing Date A review of applications will begin November 15, 2026 and continue until a suitable candidate is found. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity The Department of Biological Sciences in the Faculty of Arts and Science invites applications for an entry-level, full-time, tenure-track appointment  for a Laboratory Supervisor , commencing July 1, 2027, subject to final budgetary approval. You will work with the department's instructional faculty and technical staff to ensure the effective delivery of the laboratory components of the Department's core courses BIOL 108 ( Introduction to Evolution ) and BIOL 208 ( Principles of Ecology ).  Duties will include, but are not limited to, supporting curriculum development for labs, preparation of lab manuals and lab assessments, managing course resources in MacEwan’s Learning Management System, and coordination of laboratory instructors in multi-section courses. The position will include lab instruction in BIOL 108 and BIOL 208. This position will contribute to the continued success of the Biological Sciences Major within MacEwan’s Bachelor of Science degree. You must have an MSc in Biological Sciences, with a background in general organismal biology, ecology, or a related discipline. You must also have relevant teaching and leadership experience in a biology laboratory or field environment. Effective organization, communication, and interpersonal skills will be essential. Knowledge of Universal Design for Learning (UDL) and a proven commitment to student-centered, evidence-based lab pedagogy is an asset. You will submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and teaching dossier (including recent teaching evaluations). Only shortlisted candidates will be contacted by the Department Chair to provide three (3) letters of reference sent directly from referees. Only selected candidates will be required to submit official transcripts sent directly from the institutions where you completed your degrees. Questions about this opportunity may be addressed to Dr. Kimberley Harcombe, Chair of the Department of Biological Sciences, at harcombek@macewan.ca . How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the Faculty Association collective agreement All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.10.257": {
      "title": "Dean, Faculty of Health and Community Studies",
      "description": "Dean, Faculty of Health and Community Studies - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Dean, Faculty of Health and Community Studies Faculty of Health and Community Studies Competition No. 26.10.257 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) A competitive compensation package, including an attractive base salary and excellent benefits, will be provided. The competition will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary A competitive compensation package, including an attractive base salary and excellent benefits, will be provided. Closing Date The competition will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity Reporting to the Provost & Vice-President, Academic, the Dean, Health and Community Studies is the chief academic and operational leader of the Faculty and is responsible for its academic and administrative direction. The Dean provides dynamic and visionary leadership and advocacy on behalf of the Faculty, within the University, and beyond. The role requires both intellectual leadership and organizational creativity. The Dean promotes teaching and scholarly excellence, advances research, and nurtures mutually beneficial relationships internally and externally, and effectively manages the Faculty’s resources. The Dean will have the demonstrated ability to assess broad and diverse interests, show commitment across multiple stakeholder groups, and balance informed decision-making with consultation. The Dean will engage and inspire students, faculty, staff, and alumni, and have the capacity to develop collaborative partnerships with government and community partners throughout Edmonton and the surrounding area. Recognized as an inclusive leader and excellent communicator, the Dean will support access to education that aligns with MacEwan’s commitment to the principles of Indigeneity and reconciliation, of equity, diversity, and inclusion, innovation, and of connection, partnership, and place. Relationships Reports to: Provost & Vice-President, Academic Interacts with: President and other Senior Administrators Students and Alumni Board of Governors Deans and Associate Deans of other Faculties and Schools Government and Community Agencies and Internship Partners Accreditation, Associations, and Regulatory Bodies Leaders in the Alberta Health Community Direct Reports: Associate Deans Department Chairs Administrative Team Faculty and Staff Key Roles & Responsibilities Leadership Through an inclusive consultation process, develop and articulate a vision in alignment with MacEwan’s values and goals. Foster a culture of collegial decision-making and guide the Faculty through a period of academic governance maturation. Proactively work across the Faculty to drive and support growth for all programs. Work collaboratively with faculty, departments, and other Deans, to develop innovative new credentials to remain competitive and relevant, and to differentiate the FHCS’s offerings in an increasingly competitive market. Facilitate the advancement of faculty and staff by involving them in opportunities for professional growth and mentoring them in their teaching, scholarly, and service activities. Provide a positive and supportive environment in which people from many different backgrounds can work and study, recognizing the diverse personal and intellectual cultures. Address the Calls to Action in the Truth and Reconciliation Commission and foster stronger ties with Indigenous Communities. Address personnel and student situations in an accessible and fair manner. Communicate regularly with faculty, staff, and students in ways that increase interest in common issues by capitalizing on connections among people, ideas, and opportunities. Foster faculty and student participation in interdisciplinary research and interprofessional education, practice, and community engagement. Foster an environment that promotes academic and practice innovation, including the development of new educational pathways and programs that support the needs of the community. Work with the Alumni and Development office at MacEwan to lead and develop fundraising priorities for the Faculty and be an active leader and participant in achieving those fundraising goals. Student Success Promote a successful strategy for recruiting and retaining motivated and qualified students and supporting their academic and professional achievement. Work to continuously improve the student experience. Ensure a safe and accommodating learning environment for all, with particular focus on Indigenous, under-represented, and marginalized students. Understand and promote awareness of student services to students, including the importance of mental health supports. Encourage the participation of students on governance bodies within the Faculty and across campus. General Management Plan and prioritize personnel needs for the Faculty and establish strategies to enhance recruitment, mentorship, retention, and equity of high-calibre faculty and staff. Foster a climate and culture that stimulates all to achieve the highest standards of the professoriate. Adopt effective and transparent processes to address personnel issues. Strengthen the Faculty’s financial position through effective budget management, entrepreneurial activity, and internal and external partnership development. Manage the Faculty’s financial and human resources; provide support and direction to professional and administrative staff. Able to work within the two collective agreements; comfortable working through those processes. Provide strong support in the accreditation process and understand the various needs within the differing accrediting bodies. Advocacy and External Relations Cultivate relationships with community partners and agencies to provide opportunities for faculty and excellent practice placements for students as a key element in their educational experience. Foster excellent external relations with all relevant stakeholder groups locally, provincially, nationally, and internationally. Advocate for the Faculty on university committees and externally with professional bodies and provincial and federal governments; demonstrate political know-how and strategic approaches to interactions. Advocate for the Faculty within the institution. Teaching and Learning Promote and support the Faculty’s reputation for teaching excellence as the core element of faculty career success and student academic achievement. Oversee the development and regular evaluation of new credentials with a view to encouraging improvement and innovation while ensuring their relevance and quality. Find new opportunities to incorporate hybrid learning and innovative delivery models throughout the Faculty, ensuring strong support for programming excellence and teaching throughout. Research and Scholarship Promote excellence and integrity in research and scholarship. Foster a climate that uncovers new threads of inquiry and prominence. Encourage and enhance FHCS’s capacity and reputation for diverse and significant scholarly productivity. Promote and develop capacity for innovation in interdisciplinary research and programming, knowledge translation, and professional skills training. Recruit new faculty whose research agendas support the areas of prominent scholarship in FHCS. Communicate and celebrate research in FHCS across campus, the province, and the country. Support and mentor new tenure-track faculty in a shared commitment to community-based research and an emphasis on the scholarship of teaching and learning. The Person The ideal candidate will have excellent academic qualifications, a strong record of administrative and leadership experience, and a passion for advancing education, research/scholarship, and professional activity. Professional Experience and Qualifications MacEwan University recognizes that no one individual is likely to meet all the following criteria in equal measure; however, the following background, experience and personal qualities will be sought in candidates: Outstanding leadership skills, with an ability to inspire and mobilize others. Demonstrated commitment to the well-being, academic advancement, and success of students. Demonstrated commitment to excellence in education and ability to mentor and encourage faculty in scholarly and professional activity. Ability to think strategically and to communicate effectively. A proven record of community engagement and community-engaged scholarship. Demonstrated experience working with one or some of the professional regulating bodies in which the programs of the Faculty operate. Experience and/or an understanding of the accreditation process. Experience as an administrator and supervisor in a student-focused institution. A collaborative leadership style with the ability to encourage others to participate in collegial governance and decision-making. Experience working in a unionized environment. Experience in developing or contributing to academic planning at the Faculty or institutional level. An open communication style that inspires, engages, and encourages collaboration and partnership. Evidence of strong interpersonal and relationship-building skills and an ability to foster a positive and supportive work environment. Demonstrated success in fostering innovative solutions to address academic or administrative challenges. A strong record of teaching, scholarship, and service to qualify for an appointment as full professor, with a terminal degree in a field related to the areas of study in the Faculty. Personal and Leadership Attributes Strategic and Values-Based Leadership: A principled, thoughtful leader who approaches decisions through a values-based lens, guided by ethics, honesty, integrity, and accountability. Demonstrates sound judgment and balances collaboration with decisiveness, seeking input from others while confidently making difficult decisions when circumstances require clear direction. Relationship-Centred and Collaborative: An exceptional relationship builder who establishes trust and credibility with a diverse range of partner groups internal and external to the faculty. Skilled at finding common ground and fostering meaningful partnerships within the Faculty, across the university, and with external communities and organizations. Leads through respectful engagement, open communication, and a genuine commitment to shared success. People Leadership and Influence: A strong people leader with proven abilities in team development, influence, coaching, and conflict resolution. Creates inclusive and supportive environments where individuals feel valued, heard, and empowered to contribute their best. Accessible, approachable, and highly engaged, with a leadership style that encourages collaboration and strengthens organizational culture. Visionary, Innovative, and Forward-Looking: An innovative and intelligent thinker who embraces new ideas while remaining grounded in practical realities. Combines optimism with pragmatism, identifying opportunities for growth and improvement while maintaining focus on achievable outcomes. Energetic and enthusiastic, with a natural drive to move initiatives forward and inspire momentum across teams. Adaptable and Organizationally Savvy: Comfortable navigating complexity and working effectively in dynamic and evolving environments. Politically astute and diplomatic, with a strong understanding of organizational contexts and various perspectives. Demonstrates the agility and resilience needed to lead through change while maintaining alignment with institutional priorities and goals. Commitment to the FHCS Mission: Deeply appreciative of and respectful toward the breadth, diversity, and unique strengths of FHCS and its service offerings. Champions the value of interdisciplinary collaboration and is committed to advancing the Faculty's mission through partnership, innovation, and a shared sense of purpose. Authentic and Engaging Presence: Leads with authenticity, humility, and a positive outlook. Brings enthusiasm, approachability, and a healthy sense of humour to the workplace, fostering strong connections and creating an environment where people enjoy working together toward common goals. How to Apply Leaders International values diversity, equity, and inclusion in all aspects of our operations. Candidates are invited to contact us directly with any accommodation requests. To apply, please email your cover letter and resume (PDF or Word document only—preferably as one document) to Ardyce Kouri or Olesia Linkevych at apply@leadersinternational.com , indicating the job title in the subject line. Leaders International Executive Search | www.leadersinternational.com Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.10.256": {
      "title": "Lifeguard/Instructor",
      "description": "Lifeguard/Instructor - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Lifeguard/Instructor Sport and Wellness, Campus Services Competition No. 26.10.256 Category Salary Closing Date Casual (less than 35 hours per week) MSU Band C (Steps 1-4): $24.256 - $28.479 per hour. November 5, 2026 Category Casual (less than 35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band C (Steps 1-4): $24.256 - $28.479 per hour. Closing Date November 5, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking Lifeguard/Instructors for up to 5 casual opportunities with our Sport and Wellness department. Reporting to the Aquatics Supervisor, you will ensure the safety of all patrons in and around the aquatic facility and provide high-quality aquatic program instruction to individuals of varying skill levels, playing a key role in maintaining and promoting an aquatic environment that is enjoyable, welcoming, educational, and safe. Key responsibilities include: Monitoring pool and surrounding areas to ensure the safety of all patrons, enforcing safety policies, protocols, and surveillance; Addressing unsafe behaviours and educating patrons on safe behaviours and practices; Responding to first aid, incidents, accidents, and other emergency situations, ensuring proper first aid and rescue protocols are followed, and that required documentation is completed; Maintaining a clean and safe environment in and around the water for users by completing regular required maintenance tasks; Inspecting and maintaining safety equipment and reporting any issues; Supporting the Head Lifeguard/Instructor in completing daily operational checks and mechanical tasks; Providing high-quality instruction of all assigned aquatic programs to patrons of all skill levels, including swimming lessons, private lessons, specialty programs, and aquatic fitness; Completing lesson plans, report cards, worksheets, and attendance reports; and Communicating with parents, guardians, or participants about progress and any concerns. Skills You will have: Strong swimming ability and knowledge of principles, practices, and techniques in water safety and lifesaving activities; Knowledge of public health, safety and sanitary regulations and operational guidelines applicable to swimming pool operations; Strong written and verbal communication skills, with a commitment to customer service and the ability to work with a diverse range of clients; A positive attitude and strong interpersonal skills, with the ability to maintain a proactive approach and work both independently with minimal supervision and collaboratively within a team; Excellent organizational, problem-solving and time management skills; The ability to remain calm and make decisions quickly in high-pressure and stressful situations; and A commitment to ongoing learning and skill development. Qualifications A minimum of a high school diploma, or working towards the completion of a high school diploma; Certified in Lifesaving Society National Lifeguard (NL) and Intermediate First Aid with CPR-C and Automated External Defibrillator (AED), with the ability to renew annually or as required. Certified in Lifesaving Society Swim and Lifesaving Instructor and Lifesaving Society Oxygen Administration or progressing towards certification with completion by your hire date. Certification in advanced Lifesaving Society Leadership Courses like National Lifeguard Instructor, First Aid Instructor and Trainer would be considered an asset. Pool Operator, AFLCA or other Aquatic Fitness training, and NCCP or Lifesaving Sport or Recreational Coach certifications would all be considered assets. Aquatic experience as a lifeguard and instructor of Lifesaving Society programs is considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Position Requirements This position is on campus only. Minimum age of 15 years old. The ability to work flexible hours, which includes early mornings, evenings, and weekends. Work schedules may rotate from time to time and would not be consistent. Required to attend training and events that could fall outside of normal working hours, with sufficient notice provided. The successful incumbent will be required to obtain a Police Record Check with a Vulnerable Sector Check at their own cost. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.10.262": {
      "title": "Senior Budget Officer",
      "description": "Senior Budget Officer - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Senior Budget Officer Budget and Resource Planning, Financial Services Competition No. 26.10.262 Posting Date October 23, 2026 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) MSU Band G (Steps 1-8): $41.674 - $60.619 per hour. $75,846 - $110,326 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). November 11, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band G (Steps 1-8): $41.674 - $60.619 per hour. $75,846 - $110,326 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). Closing Date November 11, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking a Senior Budget Officer for a full-time continuing opportunity with the Budget and Resource Planning department. The Senior Budget Officer is responsible for providing budget and planning leadership and support to all departments, schools, and faculties across the university, facilitating the adoption of best practices and strengthening alignment with university’s financial goals and priorities. You will work collaboratively with leaders and budget officers on all budgetary matters, quarterly forecasts, compliance, coordination of the annual strategic budget process, and support for the development of the three-year financial plan. Key responsibilities include: Budget and Resource Management Serving as the budget officer for the central university department, responsible for budgeting, quarterly forecasting, and analysis of grants, tuition, fees, and other key financial drivers. Supporting capital project budgeting and forecasting, including expenditure projections and forecasting of capital contribution funding. Understanding the business operations of the university, Alberta’s post-secondary funding model and its respective financial accounting impact, including modelling the financial impact of changes in legislation, regulations, and policy; Supporting effective workforce management and its alignment with the organization’s strategic objectives by analyzing changes to staffing costs (step increases, cost of living adjustments, and collective bargaining agreements) and managing vacancies on an aggregate level; and Working with collective bargaining teams to provide financial modelling and costing information during collective agreement negotiations. Support the development and continuous improvement of budgeting, forecasting, reporting, and financial planning processes, tools, and systems. Reporting, Analysis, and Compliance Preparing complex, detailed financial analysis and reports that accurately report the university's financial operating and capital budgets throughout the annual budget development cycle to ensure a comprehensive, cohesive, and accurate representation of the university’s approved budget plan; Overseeing the consolidation of the university’s three-year financial plan, which is critical to maintaining financial accountability and alignment with institutional budgetary goals; and Ensuring accurate and timely reporting and monitoring of the university’s overall salary and benefits budget, which includes oversight of departments, schools, and faculties to ensure financial accountability and alignment of individual position budgets with institutional budgetary goals. Leadership and Relationship Management Supervising, training, and coaching staff, fostering a culture of collaboration and continuous improvement and learning; Prioritizing, assigning, monitoring assignments and projects to ensure efficiency, deadlines, and requirements are met by balancing and adjusting workloads or shifting resources; and Delivering both positive reinforcement and constructive feedback to support employee development and performance, escalating concerns to the Director when necessary. Project Management and Financial Reporting Reviewing the financial information for all non-capital projects to ensure they are properly reported, monitored, and kept up to date; and Ensuring non-capital budget and forecast data are accurately maintained and integrated with the University's financial and operational systems. Skills You will have: Advanced knowledge of financial administration, monitoring, forecasting, costing, and budgeting concepts and best practices; Understanding of regulatory, legislative, and compliance reporting, including the Public Sector Accounting Standards (PSAS) or International Financial Reporting Standards (IFRS); The ability to communicate professionally and effectively on sensitive and confidential matters; The ability to synthesize financial and non-financial data to assess operational performance and effectiveness; The ability to assist in the preparation of briefing materials that translate financial data into meaningful insights for decision-makers; The ability to present financial information and concepts, both verbally and in writing, to various audiences across all levels of the university, including those without financial backgrounds; Strong analysis and problem-solving skills with the ability to translate business requirements into workable processes; Excellent organization and time management skills with the ability to establish priorities, manage multiple demands, and meet deadlines; The ability to work in a dynamic and fast-paced environment, especially during peak times of year; Strong attention to detail and accuracy; Demonstrated ability to work independently and collaboratively to meet objectives and provide a high level of service to internal and external stakeholders; and Advanced working knowledge of Microsoft Office to create and manage complex spreadsheets in Excel. Qualifications A bachelor’s degree in ​business, finance,​ accounting, or a related field. A minimum of 7 years of experience in progressively responsible accounting positions in medium or large organizations. Completion or near completion of a CPA designation. Experience preparing and overseeing budget and forecast submissions in a complex environment. Experience working with financial information systems, reporting tools, and software such as Excel, Power BI, Enterprise Performance Management (EPM), PeopleSoft or similar systems. Experience in a post-secondary or public sector environment would be considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.10.269": {
      "title": "Senior Database Administrator",
      "description": "Senior Database Administrator - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Senior Database Administrator Information Technology Services Competition No. 26.10.269 Posting Date October 23, 2026 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) MSU Band G (Steps 1-8): $41.674 - $60.619 per hour. $75,846 - $110,326 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). The competition will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band G (Steps 1-8): $41.674 - $60.619 per hour. $75,846 - $110,326 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). Closing Date The competition will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking a Senior Database Administrator for a full-time continuing opportunity with Information Technology Services. Reporting to the Team Lead, IT Data and Analytics, the Senior Database Administrator is the technical subject matter expert responsible for the administration, availability, security, performance, and lifecycle management of the University’s Oracle, SQL Server, and other database environments. The role also supports PeopleSoft administration and, as operational priorities require, other enterprise database and data platforms. Key responsibilities include: Administering, maintaining, monitoring, and optimizing Oracle databases hosted in AWS RDS and Oracle applications that support critical University services; Managing database availability, security, backup and recovery, patching, upgrades, capacity planning, performance tuning, and disaster-recovery readiness; Troubleshooting complex Oracle database issues, including SQL performance, indexing, data integrity, integrations, and production incidents; Planning and executing PeopleSoft code migrations, refreshes, upgrades, and lifecycle-management activities across on-premises and cloud environments; Supporting PeopleSoft administration, including environment management, application and PeopleTools upgrades, patching, migrations, and technical troubleshooting; Collaborating with application teams, infrastructure teams, vendors, and business stakeholders to ensure reliable and secure operation of Oracle and PeopleSoft environments; Maintaining technical documentation, operational procedures, standards, and automation for database and application administration; Providing support for Microsoft SQL Server, Azure SQL, other AWS database services, and related enterprise data platforms; and Providing support for Microsoft Fabric, Azure Data Factory, data warehousing, ETL pipelines, and legacy data-integration tools, as operational priorities require. Skills You will have: Comprehensive knowledge of Oracle database administration principles, architectures, and best practices; Strong knowledge of Oracle database security, access controls, auditing, backup and recovery, patching, upgrades, capacity planning, and disaster recovery; Excellent SQL and PL/SQL skills, including query optimization, indexing, execution-plan analysis, and performance tuning; Demonstrated ability to monitor, troubleshoot, and resolve complex database availability, performance, integration, and data-integrity issues in production environments; Knowledge of AWS RDS for Oracle administration, including monitoring, configuration, snapshots, restoration, maintenance, and upgrades; Knowledge of database migration, refresh, conversion, and lifecycle-management practices; Knowledge of PeopleSoft administration, including PeopleTools, environment management, patching, upgrades, migrations, and technical troubleshooting; Familiarity with Microsoft SQL Server, Azure SQL, PostgreSQL, and other cloud-hosted database services; Familiarity with Microsoft Fabric, Azure Data Factory, data warehousing, ETL pipelines, and related data-integration technologies; Ability to develop and maintain technical documentation, operational procedures, standards, and administrative automation; Excellent analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to manage competing operational priorities; and Strong interpersonal and written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to collaborate effectively with technical teams, vendors, and business stakeholders. Qualifications A minimum of a bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field. A minimum of seven years of progressive information technology experience, including at least three years of hands-on Oracle database administration experience, including: Administering Oracle databases in production environments; Administering Microsoft SQL Server databases in production environments; Managing database security, backup and recovery, patching, upgrades, capacity, and disaster-recovery readiness; Monitoring and tuning database performance, including SQL optimization, execution-plan analysis, and indexing; Troubleshooting database availability, performance, integration, and data-integrity issues; Performing database migrations, refreshes, conversions, and lifecycle-management activities; and Administering Oracle databases in AWS RDS or a comparable cloud environment. Experience supporting PeopleSoft environments, including PeopleTools, environment management, patching, upgrades, migrations, and technical troubleshooting. Experience developing administrative automation using scripting or related tools. The following would be considered an asset: Experience administering Azure SQL, PostgreSQL, or other cloud-hosted database services; Experience with Microsoft Fabric, Azure Data Factory, ETL pipelines, data warehousing, or related data-integration technologies; Experience working in a post-secondary or public-sector environment; Oracle Database Administrator certification; AWS certification; and PeopleSoft or PeopleTools training or certification. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.10.270": {
      "title": "Budget and Accounting Technician (Internal only)",
      "description": "Budget and Accounting Technician (Internal only) - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Budget and Accounting Technician (Internal only) Budget and Resource Planning, Financial Services Competition No. 26.10.270 Posting Date October 27, 2026 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) MSU Band D (Steps 1-8): $28.501 - $41.449 per hour. $51,872 - $75,438 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). November 3, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band D (Steps 1-8): $28.501 - $41.449 per hour. $51,872 - $75,438 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). Closing Date November 3, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking a Budget and Accounting Technician for a full-time continuing opportunity with our Budget and Resource Planning Department. The Budget and Accounting Technician is accountable for contributing to the success of the University's mission by providing technical, financial, and administrative support to both the Budget and Resource Planning and Accounts Receivable functions. You will provide financial, budgeting, reporting, and administrative support to the Budget and Resource Planning team for assigned portfolios. Key responsibilities include: Budget Administration and Financial Support Supporting the preparation, maintenance, and monitoring of operating budgets for assigned portfolios; Contributing to the maintenance of budget working papers, supplementary, sorting, scheduling documentations, and financial records to ensure accuracy and completeness of budget and forecast information; Assisting with the preparation of annual budgets, quarterly forecasts, variance reports, and year-end financial reviews for assigned portfolios; Monitoring budget transactions and commitments within assigned portfolios to ensure expenditures are recorded appropriately and identifies discrepancies for review by the Financial Analyst or Senior Budget Officer; Preparing routine financial reports and reconciliations and assisting with gathering, validating, and organizing financial information required for budget planning and analysis within assigned portfolios; and Position Management and Reporting Supporting the administration and monitoring of staffing budgets and position information across assigned portfolios; Maintaining position tracking schedules and staffing reports, including vacancies, new positions, reclassifications, organizational changes, and temporary staffing arrangements within assigned portfolios; Assisting with salary forecasting by maintaining staffing data, updating workforce planning tools, and monitoring position-related financial commitments across assigned portfolios; and Supporting the collection, compilation, validation, and analysis of data used in budget planning, forecasting, and reporting activities for assigned portfolios. Billing and Accounts Receivable Providing accounts receivable and billing support in accordance with University policies, procedures, and established financial controls; Preparing and processing invoices for goods and services provided by the University and ensuring supporting documentation is complete and accurate; Monitoring outstanding accounts and performing collection activities, including account follow-up, documentation of collection efforts, and preparation of adjusting entries as required; and Preparing accounts receivable aging and dunning reports for review and generates past-due notifications for distribution to individuals and organizations. Receive and Process Payments Processing and recording payments received by the University and ensuring transactions are coded accurately and recorded in the appropriate financial systems; and Receiving, recording, and depositing funds received by the University in accordance with established procedures and internal controls. This position is for internal candidates only. Skills You will have: Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to investigate discrepancies, reconcile information, and identify solutions; The ability to synthesize financial and non-financial information and communicate findings effectively to both financial and non-financial stakeholders; Strong customer service, interpersonal, and communication skills with the ability to build positive working relationships with departments, students, employees, and external customers; The ability to organize, prioritize, and manage multiple competing deadlines during forecasting, budgeting, reporting, and accounts receivable cycles; Demonstrated ability to work independently and as part of a team while exercising sound judgment and initiative; Strong attention to detail and commitment to maintaining accurate financial and position-related records; The ability to maintain confidentiality and professionalism when handling sensitive financial and staffing information; Systems thinking skills to support continuous improvement of financial processes, workflows, and reporting tools; The ability to adapt to changing priorities and work effectively in a dynamic environment; and Intermediate proficiency in Microsoft Excel and Microsoft Word; experience with database queries and reporting tools would be considered an asset. Qualifications A minimum of a post-secondary diploma in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or a related discipline. A minimum of three years' related experience in accounting, budgeting, financial reporting, accounts receivable, or a combination of these areas. Experience with accounts receivable processes, billing, collections, cash handling, account reconciliations, and financial reporting. Experience working with computerized financial systems and Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel. The following would be considered assets: Progress toward obtaining a professional accounting designation (CPA). Experience with enterprise financial systems such as PeopleSoft Financials, Human Capital Management (HCM), and Enterprise Performance Management (EPM) systems. Experience supporting budgets, position management, forecasting, or financial analysis. Experience in a post-secondary institution, public sector organization, or other complex organizational environment. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.10.265": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Cognitive Neuroscience",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Cognitive Neuroscience - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Assistant Professor, Cognitive Neuroscience Department of Psychology, Faculty of Arts and Science Competition No. 26.10.265 Posting Date October 29, 2026 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Tenure-Track Commensurate with qualifications and experience.  New hires will normally be placed within the first 8 steps of the Assistant Professor salary table. A review of applications will begin November 22, 2026, and continue until a suitable candidate is found. Category Full-Time Tenure-Track Salary Commensurate with qualifications and experience.  New hires will normally be placed within the first 8 steps of the Assistant Professor salary table. Closing Date A review of applications will begin November 22, 2026, and continue until a suitable candidate is found. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity The Department of Psychology in the Faculty of Arts and Science invites applications for an entry-level, full-time, tenure-track appointment in Cognitive Neuroscience at the rank of Assistant Professor, commencing July 1, 2027, subject to final budgetary approval. The Department offers a vibrant and growing research environment, with opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration and undergraduate research involvement through honours theses, independent studies, and research assistantships. The Department is home to the Cognition and Neuroscience Research Group (CNRG), which brings together faculty and students investigating cognition, neuroscience, and related aspects of human behaviour. Our existing research infrastructure includes EEG, eye-tracking, and motion-tracking technologies, as well as local high-performance computing infrastructure and access to national advanced research computing resources. Faculty are encouraged to develop external research collaborations, including those involving neuroimaging facilities in the Edmonton region. We welcome applicants from across the breadth of cognitive neuroscience and related fields whose research will complement and expand our existing expertise. Areas of interest may include, but are not limited to, attention, perception, memory, learning, emotion, executive functioning, decision-making, speech and language, clinical neuropsychology, and other aspects of cognition and their neural underpinnings. We are particularly interested in candidates who will foster interdisciplinary collaboration, contribute new theoretical or methodological perspectives, and build upon the Department's existing research strengths. You will join a collegial department of more than 20 full-time faculty whose teaching and research span cognitive, biological, developmental, social, and applied domains. Psychology is the largest major in the Faculty of Arts and Science, with strong student interest in courses related to cognition, brain, and behaviour. You will be expected to contribute to teaching in cognitive psychology and neuroscience, including courses such as Cognitive Psychology, Perception, Brain and Behaviour, Human Neuropsychology, and Applied Neuropharmacology, depending on your area of expertise. You will also have opportunities to teach and develop senior-level seminars in cognitive neuroscience and related topics, contribute to Introductory Psychology, and develop courses aligned with your research specialization. The ability to teach research methods or statistics will be considered an asset. You will be expected to establish an active program of scholarship that provides meaningful opportunities for undergraduate student involvement. You must have, or be close to completion of, a terminal degree in Psychology, Neuroscience, Cognitive Science, or a closely related discipline, with a specialization in cognitive neuroscience or a related field. You will demonstrate a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching and an active research program with the potential to involve undergraduate students. You will submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching dossier (including recent teaching evaluations), statement of research interests, and sample of scholarly work. Only shortlisted candidates will be contacted by the Department Chair to provide three (3) letters of reference sent directly from referees. Only selected candidates will be required to submit official transcripts sent directly from the institutions where you completed your degrees. Questions about this opportunity may be addressed to Dr. Eric Legge, Department Chair, at Eric.Legge@macewan.ca . How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the Faculty Association collective agreement All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.10.267": {
      "title": "Tier 2 Canada Research Chair in Computational Biology",
      "description": "Tier 2 Canada Research Chair in Computational Biology - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Tier 2 Canada Research Chair in Computational Biology Department of Biological Sciences, Faculty of Arts and Science Competition No. 26.10.267 Posting Date October 29, 2026 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Tenure-Track Commensurate with qualifications and experience. A review of applications will begin January 3, 2027 and continue until a suitable candidate is found. Category Full-Time Tenure-Track Salary Commensurate with qualifications and experience. Closing Date A review of applications will begin January 3, 2027 and continue until a suitable candidate is found. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University’s Faculty of Arts and Science is seeking applications for a Tier 2 Canada Research Chair (CRC) in Computational Biology. We seek an emerging research leader who uses computational approaches to address important questions in the life sciences. The successful applicant will receive a full-time, probationary tenure-track position, at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor, in the Department of Biological Sciences. The position will commence July 1, 2027, subject to final budgetary approval. This position will support and build on MacEwan University’s Teaching Greatness: Strategic Vision 2030 . MacEwan University, in the heart of downtown Edmonton, is dedicated to providing undergraduate students with a transformative, academically rigorous, and personal learning experience in a creative, collaborative, and supportive learning environment. MacEwan continues to evolve and adapt to meet the changing needs of its students and the communities it serves, offers student-focused instruction, and inspires students through a powerful combination of academic excellence and personal learning opportunities. The Department of Biological Sciences is seeking a candidate whose research falls broadly within computational biology, including but not limited to bioinformatics, multi-omics analysis, computational ecology, mathematical and computational modelling of biological systems, or big data applications in the life sciences. Upon starting the academic appointment, the successful applicant will work with the University to apply for a Tier 2 Canada Research Chair. For further information relating to a Tier 2 Chair, please click here . In addition to establishing a research program, the successful candidate will contribute service to the institution and to undergraduate teaching within the Department of Biological Sciences. Teaching responsibilities may include courses in bioinformatics, computational biology, biological data analysis, or other areas aligned with the candidate's expertise. The successful applicant will have a reduced teaching load during the CRC appointment. This position represents a strategic investment in computationally driven biological research and interdisciplinary scholarship at MacEwan University. The successful candidate will establish, with the support of MacEwan’s Office of Research Services, a new research institute and serve as its director. This interdisciplinary institute will bring together researchers from Departments across the institution, including Biological Sciences, Computer Science, Mathematics and Statistics, and Physical Sciences, to tackle complex biological challenges through data-intensive and computational approaches. This institute will serve as a hub for computationally-enabled biological research across the University, and will develop partnerships with external organizations such as industry, healthcare organizations, government agencies, and research institutions. In alignment with MacEwan’s mandate as an undergraduate University, the institute will support undergraduate research experiences in computational and data-driven biology. The successful candidate will be expected to develop a strategic vision for the institute and build a collaborative research community that bridges traditional disciplinary boundaries, positioning MacEwan as a leader in interdisciplinary computational life science research. As a successful applicant, you will have: a PhD in biological sciences, or a related field, with experience working with large-scale biological data sets; evidence of, or strong potential for, outstanding teaching ability and a demonstrated commitment to undergraduate teaching and mentorship; an active program of original and innovative academic research in computational biology, or a related field, and evidence of a productive research program with strong potential for external funding success; and, evidence of interdisciplinary collaboration and leadership, with strong communication and relationship-building skills. CRC Eligibility Criteria A Tier-2 CRC has a term of five years, which may be renewed once for a second five-year term. Tier 2 Chairs are intended for exceptional emerging scholars. Candidates must be ten years or less from their first independent academic research-related appointment at the time of nomination. Applicants who are more than ten years beyond their first independent academic research-related appointment, and who have career breaks, such as maternity, parental, or extended sick leave, clinical training, etc., may have their eligibility for a Tier 2 Chair assessed through the program’s Tier 2 justification process. How to Apply You should submit a cover letter outlining how you meet the requirements of a Tier 2 CRC; a curriculum vitae, a statement of research interests, including how they align with the CRC focus and how they will engage undergraduate student researchers; and a teaching dossier (including your teaching philosophy and recent teaching evaluations). To apply, please visit the MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity, and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca. This position is included under the Faculty Association collective agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.10.272": {
      "title": "Front Desk Lead",
      "description": "Front Desk Lead - Residence - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Front Desk Lead - Residence Residence Services, Campus Services Competition No. 26.10.272 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Replacement Term (35 hours per week) MSU Band C (Steps 1-8): $24.256 - $35.273 per hour. $44,147 - $64,197 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). November 12, 2026 Category Full-Time Replacement Term (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band C (Steps 1-8): $24.256 - $35.273 per hour. $44,147 - $64,197 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). Closing Date November 12, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking a Front Desk Lead – Residence for a full-time 6-month replacement term opportunity with our Residence Services department. Reporting to the Supervisor, Front Desk and Guest Services, the Front Desk Lead – Residence is responsible for coordinating the daily operations of the Residence front desk, which functions 24/7 year-round. In this role, you will oversee and support front desk staff who serve as the primary point of contact for residents, guests, and the campus community. You will also be responsible for providing ongoing coaching and training, managing and updating staff schedules, and assisting the Supervisor with recruitment activities. The Front Desk Lead plays a key role in fostering a positive, customer-focused, and solution-oriented work environment while ensuring the consistent delivery of high-quality service to all residents and guests. Key responsibilities include: Assessing and determining appropriate course and/or action when responding to concerns, issues and inquiries from students, staff, and/or public; Coordinating the scheduled audit of building keys including floor master keys, parking passes and equipment; Auditing student and guest check in packages; Following up and investigating pending tasks, events and work orders from the previous shift; Preparing and monitoring schedules, arranging shift coverage when necessary, including handling any last-minute adjustments to the schedule; Ensuring the front desk is open as scheduled, including evenings, overnights, and weekends, and that qualified staff are in place during these times; Monitoring the casual student staff, making sure all the Front Desk standard procedures and processes are firmly followed and properly carried out; Liaising with Facilities staff members, authorized third party contractors and office visitors regarding ongoing projects or work orders; and Participating in brainstorming meetings with Campus Services leaders to develop action plans that reflect the organization's strategic plan. Skills You will have: Excellent organizational and time management skills with keen attention to detail; Problem solving skills and the ability to prioritize multiple tasks; Excellent communication skills and active listening skills; Strong customer service and interpersonal skills, while taking an inclusive approach and interacting professionally with a variety of internal and external client groups, including residents and hotel guests; The ability to work independently and collaboratively as part of a team, demonstrate initiative, and take charge when necessary; The ability to maintain confidentiality and deal with situations in a professional, service-oriented, and tactful manner; Strong leadership skills; The ability to understand and follow processes; and Proficiency with Microsoft Office suite, including Word, Excel, Teams and other applications. Qualifications A minimum of a post-secondary diploma in a related field. A minimum of 2 years of progressive customer service experience. Experience as a keyholder or team lead in a hotel or hospitality setting would be considered an asset. Previous work experience in a post-secondary residence would be considered an asset. Knowledge of StarRez would be considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Position Requirements The ability to work a Monday to Friday schedule from 1:30pm to 9:30pm . The ability to share on-call coverage when needed. The ability to work flexible and varied hours as workload requires during peak periods in residence for check-in, check-out, weekends and holidays. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    }
